urn:mrr:verification:01KY4PZ1415344RA8QCAW5YG1X	1	mrr/v1alpha1	VerificationResult	urn:mrr:practice:01KY1SNY86X0GDE2N9TVZKT4YF	2026-07-22 10:46:54.845914+00	urn:mrr:agent-role:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02H	sha256:6619a301c62181f90bbbc0b88d8866c1b21a3c9cb952779fd7842ec9d7d36b73	\N	null	{"id": "urn:mrr:verification:01KY4PZ1415344RA8QCAW5YG1X", "kind": "VerificationResult", "findings": [], "revision": 1, "rationale": "All three paper abstracts, re-fetched from arXiv on 2026-07-22 and read blind, support that the model-collapse mechanism exists as described: Shumailov et al. name and demonstrate it across model classes; Alemohammad et al. confirm degradation absent sufficient fresh real data (a scoping refinement, not a contradiction); Gerstgrasser et al. explicitly confirm collapse under data replacement while showing accumulation avoids it — a scope qualification on inevitability, not a refutation of existence. 3/3 agreement with the pipeline's supports relations.", "target_id": "urn:mrr:claim:01KY1SNYN45EM4Z1VSS3S97Z2M", "confidence": 0.95, "created_at": "2026-07-22T10:46:54.845914Z", "created_by": "urn:mrr:agent-role:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02H", "api_version": "mrr/v1alpha1", "practice_id": "urn:mrr:practice:01KY1SNY86X0GDE2N9TVZKT4YF", "reviewer_id": "urn:mrr:agent-role:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02H", "target_kind": "claim", "content_hash": "sha256:6619a301c62181f90bbbc0b88d8866c1b21a3c9cb952779fd7842ec9d7d36b73", "reviewer_role": "blind primary-source verifier (K1-T06, candidate c of the 2026-07-22 owner decision)", "recommendation": "pass", "checks_performed": ["Blind protocol: verifying instance received only the charter criterion and raw source texts; no prior classification visible (freeze commits dab655c, f4136f1)", "All 15 cluster-7 works independently classified against instantiate-vs-reference-v1", "All 3 theory paper abstracts re-fetched from arXiv and independently judged on mechanism existence", "Row-by-row comparison against the pipeline's recorded classifications performed only after the returns were frozen (comparison.md)"], "verification_type": "source", "evidence_inspected": ["urn:mrr:source-record:01KY1SNYDHG2V573AEMWM2W5H3", "urn:mrr:source-record:01KY1SNYDWG3ADS9NDR1RXRMGR", "urn:mrr:source-record:01KY1SNYE5XB3WTPMWA4YZ5F86"], "independence_profile": {"code_path": "no pipeline code executed — manual blind protocol per task-packets/K1-T06.yaml (verification, not replication; MTH-014 boundary respected)", "principal": "urn:mrr:person:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02J", "model_family": "large language model, fresh isolated instance; family shared with the engineering tooling", "prompt_family": "blind verification brief (corpora/model-collapse/verification/blind-brief.md), frozen commit dab655c — a lineage distinct from every pipeline prompt", "retrieval_path": "raw decisive_move texts taken from the pinned works-atlas snapshot and paper abstracts re-fetched from arXiv on 2026-07-22 — never from the pipeline's classified corpus rows", "data_access_path": "brief-embedded material only; the blind instance had no repository, database, or web access"}, "conflicts_of_interest": ["the same responsible human (the owner) stands behind proposer, executor, and verifier instances; independence here is substantive (blind primary-source re-reading), not institutional."]}
urn:mrr:verification:01KY4RMN5CACRH52BEKZ54RXYH	1	mrr/v1alpha1	VerificationResult	urn:mrr:practice:01KY1SNY86X0GDE2N9TVZKT4YF	2026-07-22 11:16:12.07656+00	urn:mrr:agent-role:01KY4RMN5CACRH52BEKZ54RXYJ	sha256:ba90ee1821e241e3a81e35872186d916db9d6c2397527adcbbfc6d1314bd0aef	\N	null	{"id": "urn:mrr:verification:01KY4RMN5CACRH52BEKZ54RXYH", "kind": "VerificationResult", "findings": [{"severity": "material", "statement": "Ground 1 (verifier's wording, verbatim): \\"The generation count fails Step 1 as written. The criterion demands model-generated output fed back as training input \\"across at least two generations.\\" Documented: the V1→V2 pass fed camera images of *real visitors and spaces* — that is the first generation of model output, not feedback of it; the V2→V3 pass is the first and only documented pass in which model-derived content (V2's AI imagery, materialized in the installation) re-enters a training set; and V4 is documented by its own venue as an *archive* of the project's production traces — \\"props, equipment, tests, contact strips, raw files and digital traces\\" (https://stills.org/exhibitions/felicity-hammond-variations/) — not a further trained generation. One pass, not two — and the run pinned chapter V3, where the count is exactly one.\\""}, {"severity": "material", "statement": "Ground 2 (verifier's wording, verbatim): \\"The channel re-grounds itself in real data at every pass — the remedy regime of the run's own theory rows. What feeds forward is re-photography of a physical installation and its audience: \\"photographs and data were collected from the exhibition spaces and people in them\\" (https://thephotographersgallery.org.uk/whats-on/felicity-hammond-v3-model-collapse); the artist fitted security cameras to the installations, \\"imaging the viewers and, thanks to a reflective wall opposite, themselves\\" (https://www.1854.photography/2025/06/in-the-studio-felicity-hammond/). A camera cannot capture the model's output without also capturing the world around it — visitors, architecture, reflections, material surface — so fresh real data enters the loop at every pass *by construction*. Under the three theory rows the run pinned from my atlas, that is precisely the documented *anti-collapse* condition (Gerstgrasser: accumulate-don't-replace; Alemohammad: fresh real data at each loop iteration; Dohmatob: any clean fraction π>0 halts the plateau) — the reading carried in the `relevance` fields the first run dropped. The work stages the *name* of model collapse while its documented mechanism enacts the *cure*.\\""}, {"severity": "material", "statement": "Ground 3 (verifier's wording, verbatim): \\"The charter's own Step-2 boundary, applied consistently, catches V3. Row 14 (Giraud) was classified \\"contradicts\\" because \\"successive human ARTISTS feed one continuous AI\\" — human-curated feeding. Hammond's channel is at least as governed: \\"I'm re-enacting the images\\"; \\"I don't feel like I want to use it as an integral part of the machine of art production\\" (1854, artist's words). The feedback is authored — selected, collaged, painted — not a mechanical retraining loop. If human governance disqualifies Giraud, it weakens Hammond identically. (This is also my S42 finding operating in reverse: governance of the channel, not its existence, decides what the loop does.)\\""}, {"severity": "minor", "statement": "Ground 4 (verifier's wording, verbatim): \\"The artist warns against the literal reading the classification performs. \\"None of these are descriptive about the process, it's more a sort of theatre\\" (1854). Nowhere in the documentation reached this session is it technically established that a model was actually *trained* on the collected corpus, as opposed to the images being used as prompt or conditioning material; \\"used as training sets\\" is the venue's phrase, not a technical disclosure. Marked as unresolved uncertainty, cutting both ways.\\""}, {"severity": "material", "statement": "Comparison note (recording session): the pinned corpus row's classification_basis reads the decisive_move as clearing step 1 \\"across at least three named generations (V1-V4)\\"; the primary documentation reached by the verifier supports exactly one documented model-derived training pass (V2→V3) — V1→V2 fed camera images of real visitors and spaces, and V4 is documented by its own venue as an archive of production traces, not a further trained generation. The sentence carrying the difference is the venue's \\"used as training sets for each subsequent variation, including V3\\" read against Stills' description of V4. The pinned row's verification_status 'verified' is not contested here; what this record contests is the classification_basis's generation arithmetic."}], "revision": 1, "rationale": "External verdict carried verbatim: \\"Verdict on `works-hammond-v3-model-collapse` (\\"instantiates\\"): does not hold under the charter's own arithmetic. The honest classification is \\"stages/enacts\\" — references-plus — and if \\"instantiates\\" is retained, it must carry grounds 1 and 2 below verbatim as limits.\\" The verifier's own honest limit, verbatim from its trace: \\"I did not see the installations; every mechanism claim rests on the exhibiting institutions' and the artist's published accounts.\\" Composition by the recording session, declared per K1-T06 derived_decision (d): the contract's recommendation vocabulary (pass|fail|inconclusive) cannot express \\"holds only as stages/enacts, with limits\\"; 'fail' is the nearest honest value because the claim's decisive row is contested as written by the verifier (derived_decision (a)'s composition rule applied to the decisive row), with the retention-with-limits nuance carried in the findings above. The numeric confidence is likewise the recording session's declared transport mapping — the verifier stated no number; 0.8 reflects a verdict definitive on documented arithmetic (grounds 1–3, each sourced at institutional or artist primaries) with one uncertainty flagged as cutting both ways (ground 4). Under MRR-FR-075 a 'fail' against a claim already 'contested' makes no status transition; under MRR-FR-077 this record and the candidate-c blind verification (urn:mrr:verification:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02K, recommendation 'pass') stand as two independent, disagreeing records on the same claim — adjudication, if any, is a separate future governance act, deliberately not taken here.", "target_id": "urn:mrr:claim:01KY1SNYKA19APBDVN1GQ3RQFS", "confidence": 0.8, "created_at": "2026-07-22T11:16:12.076560Z", "created_by": "urn:mrr:agent-role:01KY4RMN5CACRH52BEKZ54RXYJ", "api_version": "mrr/v1alpha1", "practice_id": "urn:mrr:practice:01KY1SNY86X0GDE2N9TVZKT4YF", "reviewer_id": "urn:mrr:agent-role:01KY4RMN5CACRH52BEKZ54RXYJ", "target_kind": "claim", "content_hash": "sha256:ba90ee1821e241e3a81e35872186d916db9d6c2397527adcbbfc6d1314bd0aef", "reviewer_role": "external cross-practice verifier — the Ulysses practice (irrtum-als-methode), candidate d of the owner's 2026-07-22 decision record (Entscheidung 1); bounded review of the single 'instantiates' row (works-hammond-v3-model-collapse), taken by the practice's own decision under its standing terms (offer, not order)", "recommendation": "fail", "checks_performed": ["Bounded external review conducted entirely inside the Ulysses practice's own working session (dispatcher tick, Protocol v4); full trace committed in that practice's repository (journal/2026-07-22-hammond-review.md at irrtum-als-methode@bdb3ce73fa54e19b7c899c44f54b8e234c9e8cee) and carried verbatim into this archive (ulysses-response-verbatim.md)", "Primary documentation of all four Variations chapters retrieved live by the verifier: The Photographers' Gallery V3 exhibition page, Photoworks project page (chapters, venues, dates), 1854 Photography studio interview (the artist in her own words), Stills Edinburgh V4 page; one secondary source (Books & Boots review of V3) consulted for in