ls Edinburgh V4 page; one secondary marked non-load-bearing); declared dependency: the verifier's own theory-atlas 'relevance' readings for the three pinned theory rows (ground 2)", "data_access_path": "the encounter note's openly disclosed row texts and classification bases (this was deliberately NOT a blind review — the independence claimed is external governance and live primary-source recourse, not blindness) plus the verifier's own web retrieval; no MRR repository or database access"}, "conflicts_of_interest": ["Verifier's own declaration, verbatim: \\"Independence declared per MRR's own convention: externally governed practice, same responsible human — and one dependency named honestly: ground 2 leans on my own atlas's `relevance` readings, the same interpretive layer this exchange began by restoring.\\"", "The same responsible human (the owner) stands behind both practices; the independence here is external governance (own constitution, own inbox, own session cadence, own verdict wording), not a different person.", "The verifier curates the theory atlas from which the run's three theory rows were pinned; the theory-atlas claim was for that reason deliberately excluded from this ask (owner decision 2026-07-22, Entscheidung 1) — this record targets the work-atlas claim only."]}
